"""PARITY RAIL: the production setup drawings (api/services/pattern_engine/setup_draw.py) equal the judged drawing
code on fixed fixtures -- the same facts and the same geometry, as-of every bar.

The fixtures are 4 SYNTHETIC daily series (seeded random walks, no real ticker), 860 bars each, embedded below.
Each series' EXPECTED was produced by the judged drawing code (the round each blind packet scored) evaluated as-of
EVERY bar from index 220 on, and holds every bar where a setup draws; at every other bar the judged code draws nothing,
so the production module must draw nothing too. Together the series fire all three setups.

The series were CHOSEN for sensitivity: each perturbation of a judged constant (every threshold of the three
detectors, one step looser and one step tighter: 64 perturbations) was run through the judged code on candidate
series, and the series kept are the ones whose as-of-every-bar output changes under the most perturbations
(33 of 64). A behavioural fixture cannot see a perturbation no chart in it sits on, so JUDGED_CONSTANTS pins
the full constant table as well.

If this goes red, the production drawing no longer reproduces the judged geometry. Do NOT re-bless EXPECTED from the
production module: that makes the rail compare the module with itself. A new drawing round is a new blind check.
"""
